# Luxe Backend — AI Rules

Also read: `AGENTS.md`, `documentation/architecture.md`, full `.cursorrules`. Workflows: `.cursor/skills/` (`/new-api-entity`, `/add-api-endpoint`).

## Stack
Go · Gin · GORM · PostgreSQL · Goose · JWT · Asynq (optional Redis) · Sentry · OTEL (optional)

## Cursor skills (on-demand)

| Skill | When |
|-------|------|
| `/find-skills` | Discover/install skills (local luxe skills first) |
| `/new-api-entity` | New table + full domain (migration → Swagger) |
| `/add-api-endpoint` | New handler on existing service — no new entity |

Index: `.cursor/skills/README.md`. Frontend regen: **luxe-front** `/api-gen`.

## Layering (strict)
```
Handler → apps.Applications → Application → Domain → infrastructure/postgres (GORM)
```
- **Handlers** (`interfaces/http/handlers/`): bind DTO, validate, `c.Request.Context()`, `utils.Response` only.
- **Application** (`internal/application/`): use-case orchestration; depends on domain ports and postgres repos.
- **GORM** lives in `internal/infrastructure/postgres/` — not in handlers. Use model-based GORM queries only; no `db.Raw()` or hand-written SQL strings.

**Architecture is settled.** Extend layers in place; use `/new-api-entity` or `/add-api-endpoint`. Do not recreate `controllers/`, `routes/`, or monolithic GORM services.

## New feature order

Use `/new-api-entity` for the full checklist. Summary:

migration → model → dto → postgres repo → application → register in **`apps/wire.go`** + **`bootstrap/wire.go`** → handler → **`container.go`** → routes → swagger → tests

Single new route on existing domain → `/add-api-endpoint` instead.

## Migrations
- Path: `internal/migrations/`
- `make migrate-create name=...` then `make migrate-up`
- **Schema only** — no demo/seed product data in new migrations
- UP + DOWN, `IF NOT EXISTS`, indexes, `timestamptz`

## Swagger
Never edit `docs/docs.go`, `docs/swagger.json`, `docs/swagger.yaml` (generated, gitignored).
Edit handler `@Summary`/`@Router` comments → `make swagger` → **restart API**.

**Frontend sync:** any Swagger/DTO/route change → tell **luxe-front** agent to run `pnpm api:gen` after restart (not optional).

## Clean code
- Smallest correct diff; match surrounding style
- `context.Context` first on new service methods; `db.WithContext(ctx)`
- Constants for statuses — no magic strings
- DI via constructors; wire in `bootstrap.NewServices` / `handlers.NewContainer`
- Jobs via `infrastructure/asynq.JobQueue`, not raw goroutines for orders/shipments

## Testing
- Unit: `internal/application/*_test.go`, sqlmock when mocking DB
- Integration: `tests/integration/`, real Postgres, unique suffix per test fixture
- `DATABASE_URL` + `JWT_SECRET` for integration runs

## Before done
- Build passes; relevant tests pass
- No edits to generated `docs/`
- New code registered in `bootstrap/wire.go` and `handlers/container.go` if applicable
